      "Next request.\n",
      "\u001b[34mChief Solution Architect:\n",
      "\n",
      "Instruction: Using Tavily search, research and compare three candidate agent architectures for this zero-cloud, low-API-cost job search agent: (1) a single ReAct-style tool-calling loop, (2) a planner-executor (plan-and-solve) decomposition, and (3) a multi-agent role-based pipeline (e.g., profiler/scout/matcher/tailor). For each, document the control flow, where the local LLM is invoked, failure modes, token/API cost profile, and suitability for a single-user offline deployment.\n",
      "\n",
      "Input: The memory decision is converging on a single-file SQLite core (relational profile + FTS5 + sqlite-vec) with local Ollama embeddings and a lightweight graph edge table. Tavily must be scoped strictly to live job-data fetches. Evaluate architectures against: latency, debuggability, offline resilience, and minimization of API calls.\n",
      "\u001b[32mEnterprise AI Architect:\n",
      "\n",
      "Solution: Below is the researched comparison of the **three candidate agent architectures** for your zero-cloud, low-API-cost job search agent. I grounded it in current 2025–2026 sources on agent memory/runtime design (Hindsight's self-hosted memory survey, the TypeScript/sqlite-vec multi-tier memory pattern, the hybrid FTS5+sqlite-vec+RRF design, the MemGPT/Letta control-flow model, and the local resume-tailoring agent pattern), and evaluated each against your four decision criteria: **latency, debuggability, offline resilience, and minimization of API calls** — with the memory decision (single-file SQLite core + local Ollama embeddings + lightweight graph edge table, Tavily only for live job fetches) assumed fixed.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## 0. SHARED INVARIANTS (common to all three architectures)\n",
      "\n",
      "Before comparing, these are constant across designs and they bound the analysis:\n",
      "\n",
      "| Invariant | Implementation | Consequence for architecture choice |\n",
      "|---|---|---|\n",
      "| LLM | One local model under **Ollama** (e.g., Qwen3 tool-calling class) | Every \"LLM call\" is a **local, zero-API-cost** call — but still consumes latency + CPU/GPU. Cost minimization means **minimizing *number* of inference passes**, not dollars. |\n",
      "| Embeddings | **Local** (nomic-embed-text 274 MB / qwen3-embedding:0.6b) | Embedding for memory is never an API call |\n",
      "| Memory | **SQLite** = relational profile + FTS5 + `sqlite-vec` (hybrid, RRF) + graph edge table | Retrieval is a **local function call**, sub-ms to low-ms |\n",
      "| Web | **Tavily**, scoped *only* to live job-data fetches | Tavily call count = hard cost unit; architecture must **batch and cache** it |\n",
      "| Persistence | Single `.db` file, ACID | Session continuity is free |\n",
      "\n",
      "So the real currency is: **number of LLM inference passes + number of Tavily calls + wall-clock latency + human debugging effort.**\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## 1. ARCHITECTURE A — SINGLE ReAct-STYLE TOOL-CALLING LOOP\n",
      "\n",
      "**Control flow**\n",
      "```\n",
      "User turn → [LLM \"thought\"] → choose tool → execute tool → [observe] →\n",
      "append to scratchpad → loop [LLM \"thought\"] → ... → final answer (no tool)\n",
      "```\n",
      "\n",
      "The LLM is invoked **once per loop iteration** (each Thought→Action step). It sees a growing scratchpad of prior thoughts/observations. Termination is model-decided (\"I have enough\").\n",
      "\n",
      "**Where the local LLM is invoked**\n",
      "- 1 inference pass **per tool decision**, plus 1 final synthesis pass.\n",
      "- Typical loop depth for \"find me remote senior backend roles matching my profile\": 3–8 iterations → **4–9 LLM passes per request.**\n",
      "\n",
      "**Token / API cost profile**\n",
      "- **No per-call $$ API cost** (local), but token *volume* grows ~linearly with loop depth because the full scratchpad is re-sent each iteration (**context re-send tax**).\n",
      "- **Tavily:** naturally 1 call per scout iteration → risk of *repeated* fetches. Must be tamed by a **cache-first tool wrapper** (see §5).\n",
      "- Net: cheapest *integration* effort, most volatile token/time budget.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Failure modes**\n",
      "| Failure | Mechanism | Mitigation |\n",
      "|---|---|---|\n",
      "| **Loop divergence / non-termination** | Model keeps calling tools | Hard `max_iterations` cap + no-progress detector |\n",
      "| **Thrashing on Tavily** | Re-fetches same/similar query | Deterministic query-hash cache in SQLite; tool refuses duplicate within TTL |\n",
      "| **Tool-arg hallucination** | Bad JSON, wrong tool | Strict schema validation + repair/retry (costs 1 extra pass) |\n",
      "| **Context overflow** | Scratchpad balloons on long sessions | Summarize/compact scratchpad (a *local* LLM pass) |\n",
      "| **Silent profile drift** | Model writes memory without you noticing | Gate writes behind typed profile schema |\n",
      "\n",
      "**Suitability for single-user offline**\n",
      "- ✅ **Highest** conceptual simplicity; runs on any Ollama box; easy to demo.\n",
      "- ⚠️ Latency and token budget grow with task complexity; the same \"flexibility\" that helps exploration hurts **predictability**.\n",
      "- ✅ **Best first architecture** for an MVP because almost everything is one process + one SQLite file.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## 2. ARCHITECTURE B — PLANNER–EXECUTOR (PLAN-AND-SOLVE) DECOMPOSITION\n",
      "\n",
      "**Control flow**\n",
      "```\n",
      "User turn → [Planner LLM]] → emit explicit DAG/plan (steps + tool intent) →\n",
      "Executor runs steps deterministically (no LLM per step unless needed) →\n",
      "[Verifier/synthesis LLM] → final answer → optional replan on failure\n",
      "```\n",
      "\n",
      "Two distinct LLM roles: **Planner** (1 call, maybe 2–3 on replan) and **Synthesizer** (1 call). The middle execution is largely **non-LLM** — SQL reads, vector search, Tavily fetch, ranking math.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Where the local LLM is invoked**\n",
      "- 1 planner pass + 1 synthesis pass + (occasionally) 1 replan pass → **2–4 LLM passes total**, *independent of task length* because the plan is fixed up front.\n",
      "- Tools are called by **deterministic executor code**, not by the model.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Token / API cost profile**\n",
      "- **Lowest token volume** of the three for complex/multi-step tasks: the expensive context is built *once* at plan time, then execution is code.\n",
      "- **Tavily:** can be **batched** in a single planned step (\"fetch latest postings for these 3 role queries\") → fewest API calls. Ideal for your \"Tavily scoped strictly to live job-data fetches\" rule.\n",
      "- Trade-off: plan may be **wrong/incomplete** → replan costs passes; brittle if task shape varies a lot.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Failure modes**\n",
      "| Failure | Mechanism | Mitigation |\n",
      "|---|---|---|\n",
      "| **Bad plan / under-decomposition** | Planner omits needed step | Verifier agent + bounded replan; few-shot plan templates for job-search |\n",
      "| **Over-rigid execution** | World changes mid-run | Allow executor to flag \"replan required\" |\n",
      "| **Cascading plan error** | Step 2 assumes step 1 output that changed | Schema-validate inter-step contracts |\n",
      "| **Planner prompt complexity** | Hard to get robust plans | Constrain to a **library of known plan templates** (highly effective for a *domain-specific* agent) |\n",
      "| **Debugging split-brain** | Bug is in plan vs. executor | — actually a *strength*: plan is an inspectable artifact |\n",
      "\n",
      "**Suitability for single-user offline**\n",
      "- ✅ **Best cost/latency predictability** — fewest LLM passes, fewest Tavily calls.\n",
      "- ✅ **Best debuggability at scale**: the plan is a declarative, loggable object; you can replay/unit-test the executor with a frozen plan — no LLM in the loop.\n",
      "- ⚠️ Slightly more engineering (plan schema, executor, verifier).\n",
      "- ✅ **Strong fit** because job-search is a **templatable, repeatable domain** (profile → scout → rank → tailor), which is exactly where plan-and-solve shines.\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "## 3. ARCHITECTURE C — MULTI-AGENT ROLE-BASED PIPELINE\n",
      "\n",
      "**Control flow**\n",
      "```\n",
      "Profiler → Scout → Matcher → Tailor → (Critic/Verifier)\n",
      "   ↑ each is its own prompt+role, passing structured artifacts, orchestrated by code or a supervisor\n",
      "```\n",
      "Roles map to your domain:\n",
      "- **Profiler**: reads/updates the SQLite profile + graph (skills, target roles, constraints).\n",
      "- **Scout**: calls **Tavily** (only role allowed to touch the web) → writes postings into SQLite cache.\n",
      "- **Matcher**: hybrid retrieval (FTS5 ∥ sqlite-vec ∥ graph) + local scoring/ranking.\n",
      "- **Tailor**: generates tailored resume bullets/cover note.\n",
      "- **Critic** (optional): ATS/keyword/consistency check.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Where the local LLM is invoked**\n",
      "- **Per role, per invocation** → typically **4–6 LLM passes per request** (one per agent, more if a role loops or retries). Each role has a **narrower, single-purpose prompt** (a quality advantage).\n",
      "- Some roles (Matcher ranking) can be **mostly deterministic**, cutting passes.\n",
      "\n",
      "**Token / API cost profile**\n",
      "- **Highest structural overhead** if each role re-loads context; mitigated because each prompt is **small and role-scoped** (less per-call context than a single ReAct scratchpad).\n",
      "- **Tavily:** cleanly **isolated to Scout** → easiest architecture to *enforce* minimal, batched web calls. This is its standout advantage for your constraint.\n",
      "- Orchestration can be **sequential** (simpler, higher latency) or **parallel** (needs threads/async; local GPU serializes anyway).\n",
      "\n",
      "**Failure modes**\n",
      "| Failure | Mechanism | Mitigation |\n",
      "|---|---|---|\n",
      "| **Error propagation** | Scout misses roles → Matcher ranks garbage | Artifact schema validation between stages + Critic |\n",
      "| **Coordination overhead** | Roles disagree/loop | Deterministic orchestrator, not LLM supervisor (keep it offline-cheap) |\n",
      "| **Cost multiplication** | N roles × retries × context | Strict per-role context budgets; cache artifacts in SQLite |\n",
      "| **Debuggability gap** | Which agent erred? | ✅ Actually strong: per-role logs are clean seams |\n",
      "| **Fallback opacity** | Silently uses stale jobs | Scout writes timestamped cache; Matcher must surface freshness |\n",
      "\n",
      "**Suitability for single-user offline**\n",
